# Banter in The Drowned Crossroads (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is drowned_crossroads): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ dc_trail1_01_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dc_trail1 and not flag.vander_met
interject name:rook_coldwake: Poor drainage on this hummock, Lucan, and these cypress roots are buckled past all proper zoning. Whoever left a withered hand by the reeds never filed for burial.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, the dark has teeth behind those reeds, if you please. Though I must deduct a mark from the quarry for leaving its extremities in the mud.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Your Barnaby is crowding my boots again, and he is shaking worse than a loose headstone. Is there thunder coming, or did someone drop kettle corn in the fire?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, no, that yip is a grave omen of marsh predators, I assure you. Sit, Barnaby, stay close by the light while the watchman checks the perimeter.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the turf by that water, lad, the black mud goes down deep. Remind me to draw a breath before we turn in, or the damp will stiffen my ribs.
endif
-> END

~ dc_trail3_02_silas_tobin
if name:silas_vane and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_trail3 and not flag.dc_ghoul_done
interject name:silas_vane: Look at that smashed strongbox cart, Tobin, somebody folded hard when the dead called the bet. All that purple cloth in the mud and not a single copper left to palm.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave the mud alone, Silas, this green fog tastes of sour marrow and split iron. You breathe too much of that in and even my stitching won't hold your lungs.
interject name:silas_vane: Good thing I don't keep lungs behind these ribs, friend, though the chill is rattling through my bones something fierce. Tell's in the twitch, and those reeds aren't moving on the wind.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Nothing grows right where armed men rot under a banner, just bad seed and wet bone. Hold still, you've caught torn purple thread on your censer chain and it's fraying.
interject name:silas_vane: Let it fray, I'd rather swing bitter herbs than linger where the house cleaned everybody out. Keep walking before that fog decides we owe on the old tab.
endif
-> END

~ dc_murkwater_03_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:dc_murkwater and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at these swaying walkways, Cordelia, a whole town hung on stilts like a cheap matinee set. One slip into that black water and my hem is ruined for the season.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The structural ratio of rope to cypress is delightfully precarious, darling. More importantly, Mama Pelletier's barrels of pickled specimens by the cookshack suggest a fascinating local brine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness just tried to rhyme coffin boat with petticoat, and I am ready to drop him in a crab trap. At least Lyla Webb's stall has a few shiny buttons worth the walk.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do examine the chalked odds on the fight pit board before you spend your loose change. The pathology of the crowd by the sunk ring indicates a very high mortality rate.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Cheap seats always want blood on the sawdust, darling, it is the oldest billing in the business. Let us keep to the lanterns before the damp unpicks my cuffs.
endif
-> END

~ dc_fort_04_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:dc_fort and not flag.screams_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: This palisade is well past capacity, Cordelia, bedrolls blocking the yard and zero fire clearance. And that throne hall sofa looks cobbled together from three separate evictions.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The upholstery is an anatomical marvel of bad stitching, Rook, though I am more intrigued by the refugees' pulses. Fear has elevated every heart rate in the yard by forty percent.
interject name:rook_coldwake: You can leave their humours off the shift log, they have had a rough night without you tapping your vials. Someone even left a child's wooden boat by the rug.
interject name:cordelia_skein: A former banner repurposed as floor covering, stained with bayou mud and mild arterial spray. Vander Boone's enforcers in purple and black clearly lack a proper sanitation assay.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unruly lot, the whole garrison, lounging in cushioned chairs while the drainage fails outside. Settle down now, let us finish our business and clear the yard.
endif
-> END

~ dc_shack_05_delphine_tobin
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_shack_approach and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Warm firelight through the window and then neon magenta bottles on the shelf, what a cheap trick for the gallery. Though at three coppers a tag, the house is practically giving the props away.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep your fingers off the shelves, Delphine, the weave on these idols is twisted right against the grain. Whoever tied that reed work was stitching a canker straight into the straw.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at this woven doll on the end, Tobin, it has hands the exact size of mine. Tell me right now you did not leave one of your little poppets here.
interject name:tobin_hayward: I don't work in marsh reed, girl, and I never tag my seams for three coppers. Step back from that spiral stair, the dark down there smells of wet burlap and old hexing.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He is not laughing over my shoulder anymore, Tobin, not a single pun. Let us get out of this shack before someone reaches for our threads.
endif
-> END

~ dc_lagoon_06_tobin_lucan
if name:tobin_hayward and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dc_lagoon and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Funnels coughing magenta smoke into the mangroves, and the water tastes of drowned rust and sweet rot. That is no proper boat on the mud island, Lucan, it is a split wreck wearing paint.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A fascinating glamour upon the quarry, Tobin, though the scent of river mud and scorched oil is most uncivilised. Even Barnaby has flattened his ears at that gangplank.
interject name:tobin_hayward: My mice won't even poke their noses out of my lapels with that neon light on the water. Something steel is glowing down under the surface, right where the taproots rot.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Prime specimen of an ambush snare, if you please, dressed up with faded letters to lure the unwary. I award it three out of ten for subtle posture.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil never held water that colour, and I don't trust a plank that looks whole from only one angle. Keep your lantern low and watch your footing on the mud.
endif
-> END

~ dc_boat_promenade_07_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and at:dc_boat_promenade and not flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Green and magenta soulfire, catchy jazz, and a hundred glassy-eyed marks who won't look you in the socket. Watch your step on the promenade, Delphine, this whole top deck is a rigged shoe.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the seams, darling, I know a papier-mache headliner when I walk across one. A paddle wheel that never turns and a crocodile skull on the flag, it is terribly overdone.
interject name:silas_vane: That bellhop by the balcony hasn't blinked since we came up the gangplank. Nobody here is playing for coins, and the house doesn't let the winners walk off the boat.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Look at the revellers' cuffs, Silas, fine clothes and not a single soul inside them awake enough to clap. It is just a stage full of puppets waiting for the curtain to drop.
interject name:silas_vane: Then keep your hands out of your pockets and don't call the tune. We take one look over the balcony and we fold before the music stops.
endif
-> END

~ dc_lagoon_08_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:dc_lagoon and flag.grinning_sinner_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: Remarkable how quickly the magenta smoke dissipates from the funnels once the host pathology is excised. The ambient pulse of the entire lagoon has dropped to a flat zero.
interject name:tobin_hayward: The rot hasn't left the mud island, Cordelia, it just went quiet under the mangroves. Look out past the landing, it is only a split wreck with faded letters now.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My six eyes still register something steel glowing beneath the water, though the arcanum ratio is rapidly cooling. A pity, I had hoped to bottle a sample of that neon vapour.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave it in the silt where it belongs, we don't need swamp humours corked in your waistcoat. The air still smells like scorched bone, and my straw is damp through.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your primrose at the cuff appears quite unbothered by the damp, darling. Come along, let us quit the landing before the mosquitoes discover you have no blood to assay.
endif
-> END
